Isolating high-frequency arrival parameters defined explicitly mathematically marking logical stream rate $\lambda$, integrating tightly bounding kernel cache flushing interval bounds defined $\tau_{flush}$ formalizes an empirically generated geometric write batch limit modeled theoretically establishing $B_{eff}$:
\begin{equation}
B_{eff} \approx \lambda \cdot \tau_{flush}
