Guaranteeing explicitly structured $B_{eff} \gg \text{erase block capacities}$ mathematically reduces absolute geometric probabilities invoking systemic physical hardware logic loops (RMW sweeps) dramatically limiting amplification profiles entirely. Aligning multi-megabyte sequential host writes identically mimics generic analytical properties mirroring over-provisioned NVMe boundaries masking structural SD GC limitations natively.

\subsection{JEDEC Endurance Projection Mechanics}
Quantifying theoretical host-level optimizations dictates constructing verified longevity models tracking physical continuous continuous workloads natively. The standard mathematical model applies directly formulating solid-state limits defined under foundational JEDEC frameworks evaluating rigorous testing criteria (JESD218) \cite{b12}. Evaluating theoretical limits designated $C \times S$ isolating theoretical capacity arrays evaluates structural hardware geometry. The crucial modifier tracking degradation assigns functional parameters isolating combined logical operational amplification variables modeling theoretical $WAF_{total}$ representing compounded subsystem metrics isolating FS and underlying FTL geometric behaviors.

Pragmatic limitations strictly assume practical capacities explicitly withholding roughly 10\% isolating manufacturer bounds limiting system access variables preventing premature array saturation failures executing parameters:
\begin{equation}
L = \frac{0.10 \times (C \times S)}{D \times WAF_{total} \times 365}
\label{eq:lifespan}
\end{equation}

Tracking definitions logically bounding formulation parameters define:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $L$: Hardware operational expiration timeframe measured executing year spans.
    \item $C$: Fixed operational Program/Erase (P/E) failure baseline loops (3,000 for standard MLC distributions).
    \item $S$: Scaled analytical capability limits natively bounds GB thresholds (i.e., 32).
    \item $D$: Logical subsystem execution writes evaluating total GB measured explicitly across daily metrics.
    \item $WAF_{total}$: System-wide operational empirical Write Amplification Ratio boundaries.
\end{itemize}

Hardware environments natively encounter secondary reliability faults originating structurally across complex retention degradation or generic voltage read limits \cite{b10}. Establishing conservative bounds formally assigns analytical properties projecting metrics encompassing pessimistic boundary models operating explicitly assuming TLC hardware baseline failure cycles explicitly mapped against an isolated rigorous 1,000 P/E parameter baseline bounds natively.

